      "text": "First, we use the formula $\\tan(x + y) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{1 - \\tan x \\cdot \\tan y}$. Using it, we can get:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 + \\tan(20^\\circ + 5^\\circ))(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) \\\\\n&= (1 + \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 5^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 5^\\circ})(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) \\\\\n&= 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\frac{\\tan 5^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 5^\\circ} \\\\\n&= (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 5^\\circ) + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 5^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 5^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 5^\\circ} + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 5^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ \\\\\n&= 1 + \\tan 25^\\circ.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSince $1 + \\tan \\theta$ is the tangent of $45^\\circ + \\theta$, the answer is $\\boxed{2}$.",
