      "text": "First, use the double angle identity for tangent: $\\tan 50 = \\frac{2\\tan20}{1 - \\tan^2 20}.$\nSubstituting $\\tan 50$ into the expression, we have $(1 + \\tan 20)(\\tan 50 + 1).$\nExpanding the product, we get $1 + \\tan 20 + \\tan 20 \\tan 50 + \\tan 20.$\nUsing the identity $\\tan 20 \\tan 50 = 1,$ the expression simplifies to $1 + \\tan 20 + 1 + \\tan 20 = \\boxed{2}.$The answer is: 2",
